  "decision_conditions": [
    "The Local Planning Authority, having regard to its own records and the evidence submitted by the applicant, considers that the applicant has failed to demonstrate, on the balance of probability, that 29 North Circular Road, London, N13 5EG has been in continuous use as five self-contained residential flats throughout the relevant immunity period. The submitted evidence is insufficient and does not provide a complete and consistent account of the commencement and continuity of the use of each of the five flats. Accordingly, the claimed use has not been established as lawful, and the Certificate of Lawfulness for Existing Use or Development is refused."
